# TraceScope product direction (user decisions)

When the user asks what to build next, or starts a new iteration, **remind them of this direction** before proposing large new work.

## Current pillars (stable — polish, don’t expand lightly)

1. **功能影响分析**
2. **设计差异分析** — design-stack enrichment is **on hold**; the user will redesign a better approach later. Do not keep piling android-xml–style enrichments unless they reopen this.
3. **崩溃分析** — local USB capture (Android; iOS macOS-only) + Umeng + Crashlytics; dual paths **输出复现方式** (primary) / **定位并修复**.

## Explicitly deferred / don’t push

- **Web crash analysis / web-specific crash tab** — browser “crashes” are rare; web QA is functional / JS / compatibility, not USB-style crash capture. Parked.
- **Browser extension recording** — scaffold only; not current delivery.
- **Crash symbolication (mapping / dSYM)** — considered low value when AI already sees the full stack; do not prioritize.
- **Umeng OpenAPI** — paid; only if a real user asks.
- **Paste-stack / “已有堆栈？直接分析”** — removed on purpose; local capture is USB-first.
- **Windows iOS USB live capture** — not realistic short-term.

## Extend only when there is a concrete user need

- Crash sources: Sentry, Bugly, other APMs  
- Trackers: Jira, Feishu/Lark, etc.  
- Design sources: MasterGo, 即时设计, etc.  
- Crashlytics service-account full reports: follow upstream  

## Naming / UX reminders

- Local provider display name: **本机崩溃采集** (not「收件箱」).
- Prefer **输出复现方式** over deep fix for teammate handoff.
